        {
          "id": "bhhs2020e1-q14b",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "stem": "If \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\) are the roots of the equation \\(x^2+mx+n=0\\), find the roots of \\(nx^2-mx+1=0\\) in terms of \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\).",
          "hint": "Use α + β = −m, αβ = n, then compare sum and product of the new roots.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Sum and product of roots of \\(x^2+mx+n=0\\).",
              "work": "\\(\\alpha+\\beta=-m,\\qquad\\alpha\\beta=n\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Divide \\(nx^2-mx+1=0\\) by \\(n\\) and substitute.",
              "work": "\\(x^2-\\frac{m}{n}x+\\frac1n=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ x^2+\\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{\\alpha\\beta}x+\\frac{1}{\\alpha\\beta}=0\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Guess \\(-\\frac1\\alpha\\) and \\(-\\frac1\\beta\\): check their sum and product.",
              "work": "\\(-\\frac1\\alpha-\\frac1\\beta=-\\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{\\alpha\\beta},\\qquad\\left(-\\frac1\\alpha\\right)\\left(-\\frac1\\beta\\right)=\\frac{1}{\\alpha\\beta}\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "The sum must be \\(-\\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{\\alpha\\beta}\\) (= minus the \\(x\\)-coefficient) and the product \\(\\frac{1}{\\alpha\\beta}\\) — both match. So the roots are \\(-\\frac1\\alpha\\) and \\(-\\frac1\\beta\\)."
            }
          ],
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
            "source": "Baulkham Hills 2020 3U Trials & Solutions",
            "school": "Baulkham Hills High School",
            "year": 2020,
            "number": "14(b)"
          },
          "options": [
            "\\(-\\alpha\\) and \\(-\\beta\\)",
            "\\(\\alpha\\beta\\) and \\(\\alpha+\\beta\\)",
            "\\(-\\frac{1}{\\alpha}\\) and \\(-\\frac{1}{\\beta}\\)",
            "\\(\\frac{1}{\\alpha}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{\\beta}\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "find the roots of \\(nx^2-mx+1=0\\)",
              "note": "Write m and n using α and β; the new equation's sum is m/n and product 1/n."
            }
          ]
