        {
          "id": "chs2020e1-q12c",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "stem": "The polynomial equation \\(4x^3-12x^2+5x+6=0\\) has roots \\(\\alpha,\\beta\\) and \\(\\gamma\\). It is known that one of the roots is the sum of the other two. Find \\(\\alpha,\\beta\\) and \\(\\gamma\\).",
          "hint": "Let α = β + γ; the sum of roots then gives α directly.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Let \\(\\alpha=\\beta+\\gamma\\). Sum of roots \\(=-\\frac ba=3\\).",
              "work": "\\(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=3\\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\alpha+\\alpha=3\\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\alpha=\\frac32\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Product of roots \\(=-\\frac da=-\\frac64=-\\frac32\\).",
              "work": "\\(\\tfrac32\\beta\\gamma=-\\tfrac32\\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\beta\\gamma=-1\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Also \\(\\beta+\\gamma=\\alpha=\\frac32\\). So \\(\\beta,\\gamma\\) are roots of a quadratic.",
              "work": "\\(t^2-\\tfrac32t-1=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ 2t^2-3t-2=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ (2t+1)(t-2)=0\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "So the roots are",
              "work": "\\(\\alpha=\\frac32,\\quad\\beta=2,\\quad\\gamma=-\\frac12\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Check: \\(4(2)^3-12(2)^2+5(2)+6=32-48+10+6=0\\) ✓."
            }
          ],
          "xp": 1,
