        {
          "id": "chs2020e1-q14a",
          "type": "multipart",
          "stem": "The cubic equation \\(2x^3-x^2+x-1=0\\) has roots \\(\\alpha\\), \\(\\beta\\) and \\(\\gamma\\).\nShow without finding each individual root that",
          "meta": {
            "source": "Caringbah 2020 3U Trials & Solutions",
            "school": "Caringbah High School",
            "year": 2020,
            "number": "14(a)"
          },
          "parts": [
            {
              "id": "chs2020e1-q14a-i",
              "type": "review",
              "difficulty": "medium",
              "timeLimit": 60,
              "stem": "\\(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2=-\\frac34\\)",
              "hint": "Use (α + β + γ)² − 2(αβ + βγ + γα).",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "explain": "Sum and pair-sum from the coefficients \\(a=2,b=-1,c=1,d=-1\\).",
                  "work": "\\(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=-\\frac ba=\\frac12,\\qquad\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha=\\frac ca=\\frac12\\)"
                },
                {
                  "explain": "Use the identity for a sum of squares.",
                  "work": "\\(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2=(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)^2-2(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha)\\)"
                },
                {
                  "explain": "Substitute.",
                  "work": "\\(=\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)^2-2\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)=\\tfrac14-1=-\\frac34\\)"
                },
                {
                  "explain": "A negative sum of squares means some roots are not real."
                }
              ],
              "xp": 1,
              "meta": {
                "source": "Caringbah 2020 3U Trials & Solutions",
                "school": "Caringbah High School",
                "year": 2020,
                "number": "14(a)(i)"
              },
              "answer": "\\(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=\\frac12\\), \\(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha=\\frac12\\). \\(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2=(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)^2-2(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha)=\\frac14-1=-\\frac34\\).",
              "manual": true,
              "keyPoints": [
                {
                  "text": "\\(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2=-\\frac34\\)",
                  "note": "Expand (α + β + γ)² and subtract twice the pair-sum."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "chs2020e1-q14a-ii",
              "type": "review",
              "difficulty": "hard",
              "timeLimit": 60,
              "stem": "\\(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3=\\frac78\\)",
              "hint": "Substitute each root into the equation and add.",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "explain": "Each root satisfies the equation, so \\(2\\alpha^3=\\alpha^2-\\alpha+1\\), and likewise for \\(\\beta\\), \\(\\gamma\\).",
                  "work": "\\(2\\alpha^3-\\alpha^2+\\alpha-1=0\\)"
                },
                {
                  "explain": "Add the three equations.",
                  "work": "\\(2\\left(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3\\right)-\\left(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2\\right)+(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)-3=0\\)"
                },
                {
                  "explain": "Substitute (i) and the sum of roots.",
                  "work": "\\(2\\left(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3\\right)+\\frac34+\\frac12-3=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ 2\\left(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3\\right)=\\frac74\\)"
                },
                {
                  "explain": "Divide by 2.",
                  "work": "\\(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3=\\frac78\\)"
                }
              ],
              "xp": 1,
              "meta": {
                "source": "Caringbah 2020 3U Trials & Solutions",
                "school": "Caringbah High School",
                "year": 2020,
                "number": "14(a)(ii)"
              },
              "answer": "Each root satisfies \\(2x^3=x^2-x+1\\). Adding for α, β, γ: \\(2\\sum\\alpha^3=\\sum\\alpha^2-\\sum\\alpha+3=-\\frac34-\\frac12+3=\\frac74\\), so \\(\\sum\\alpha^3=\\frac78\\).",
              "manual": true,
              "keyPoints": [
                {
                  "text": "\\(\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3=\\frac78\\)",
                  "note": "Each root satisfies 2x³ − x² + x − 1 = 0; add the three versions."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
